#!/usr/bin/python3 -B
"""apt-sources module: the profile's extra apt repositories as deb822 files with fingerprint-verified keys.

    apt-sources check     exit 0 satisfied, 3 drift (read-only, no root, no network)
    apt-sources status    the same facts, one line each, plus the sources nobody declared (`unmanaged`)
    apt-sources plan      what `install` is going to do, with a diff for every text file (`--dry-run`)
    apt-sources install   as root (sudo): make them true

Options come from `[modules.apt-sources]` (UBUNTU_TWEAK_MODULE_CONFIG): `sources`, a table of tables keyed by the
source name (merges across profile.toml and machine.toml) or a list of tables with a `name`. Per source: `uris`,
`suites`, `components`, `architectures`, `types`, `key_url`, `key_urls` (mirrors), `key_cached` (armored key kept
in the profile), `key_format` (asc | gpg), `fingerprint` (REQUIRED while enabled), `pin`, `enabled`.

A key is installed only when the primary-key fingerprints of the file equal the pinned ones; keys are tried in the
order key_url, key_urls, key_cached; one failing source never blocks the others; network causes only make the
installer exit 75. `check`, `plan` and `install` all read one `inspect()`. `APT_SOURCES_ROOT=DIR` stages every path
below DIR (tests; needs no root). Spec: docs/specs/apt-sources.md.
"""

from __future__ import annotations

